                        ],
                        "form": "форпо́стах"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "cd38fc92-d70a-46ba-82d2-d73f8550f812",
                        "entry_id": "8ec3142a-f714-339f-8780-24b2da2e8a8b",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "locative"
                        ],
                        "form": "(на) форпо́сте и (на) форпосту́"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aaba746a-e8e6-37a0-891b-3c05cdd5381e",
                        "entry_id": "8ec3142a-f714-339f-8780-24b2da2e8a8b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар., воен. передовой сторожевой пост, выставляемый в целях предупреждения внезапного нападения противника; место расположения такого поста"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a37136d-4d96-4ca3-b554-436e7b5bdbc2",
                                "sense_id": "aaba746a-e8e6-37a0-891b-3c05cdd5381e",
                                "text": "Не взял ли ты кого в плен на форпосте?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bcaf39a6-b446-45ee-8edf-c9f3df63937a",
                                "sense_id": "aaba746a-e8e6-37a0-891b-3c05cdd5381e",
                                "text": "От Ачимовой до Зудиловского форпоста волок болотами или низкими полями."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dbc523d8-9e2c-3b3a-ac45-db784371446e",
                        "entry_id": "8ec3142a-f714-339f-8780-24b2da2e8a8b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. передовой пункт, опора чего-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "62b2c19d-d209-467f-8872-ac5002f53772",
                                "sense_id": "dbc523d8-9e2c-3b3a-ac45-db784371446e",
                                "text": "Чем больше народу удается притормозить уже на форпосту, тем лучше домашний врач делает свое дело."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "23a20b1e-19d8-4ac3-8741-4a17a7f26a34",
                                "sense_id": "dbc523d8-9e2c-3b3a-ac45-db784371446e",
                                "text": "Теперь я понял, что нашел крайний северо-восточный форпост Африки ― место, куда до оледенения докатилась волна переселений."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a2b1e00-6358-313d-bda5-0330bdbf0d87",
                        "entry_id": "8ec3142a-f714-339f-8780-24b2da2e8a8b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. первичная пионерская организация в 1920-х годах"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d614d5e1-c327-40a9-b9ff-1f90284815ae",
                                "sense_id": "3a2b1e00-6358-313d-bda5-0330bdbf0d87",
                                "text": "В настоящее время отряды пионеров организуются при фабриках и заводах; в школах же создаются форпосты, как органы смычки между всем коллективом школы и рабочим движением."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "352dbd97-0060-4446-ab73-8d1136c40642",
                        "source_entry_id": "8ec3142a-f714-339f-8780-24b2da2e8a8b",
                        "target_lang_word": "outpost",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "outpost",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f6722ee-b311-3ffc-a7c1-0619dd98cf09",
                                        "entry_id": "ff5e4005-f260-3bb2-a47c-09e420bdaba6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A military post stationed at a distance from the main body of troops."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49849c02-7e09-424b-9c3f-b7032b3483f4",
                                                "sense_id": "3f6722ee-b311-3ffc-a7c1-0619dd98cf09",
                                                "text": "The outpost did not have enough ammunition to resist a determined assault."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f042d053-cd7f-3bc1-b127-75daffdd94e7",
                                        "entry_id": "ff5e4005-f260-3bb2-a47c-09e420bdaba6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The body of troops manning such a post."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db477e63-f9aa-4b7d-966c-86e130cc7f6d",
                                                "sense_id": "f042d053-cd7f-3bc1-b127-75daffdd94e7",
                                                "text": "Sgt. Smith fleeced most of the rest of the outpost of their earnings in their weekly game of craps."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a0bbf21-e5c5-3e31-acf2-7686ac532e17",
                                        "entry_id": "ff5e4005-f260-3bb2-a47c-09e420bdaba6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An outlying settlement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50c47364-4311-4d65-a15c-fe94f490e35a",
                                                "sense_id": "1a0bbf21-e5c5-3e31-acf2-7686ac532e17",
                                                "text": "Beyond the border proper, there are three small outposts not officially under government protection."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ba812f5-c3e1-4ccd-9d1f-1c3718e5ed6b",
                                                "sense_id": "1a0bbf21-e5c5-3e31-acf2-7686ac532e17",
                                                "text": "On March 9, 1903, an extension, 50 miles in length, was opened from Letterkenny to the remote outpost of Burtonport, a small township on the shores of the Atlantic in the far north-west corner of Co. Donegal, running through some of the wildest and bleakest parts of the country."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78fea91e-23d8-4ca1-a9fc-db23847005fa",
                                                "sense_id": "1a0bbf21-e5c5-3e31-acf2-7686ac532e17",
                                                "text": "[…] Colonel Moen was trying to make sense of the radio nets, which had never really been operational let alone secure; our numerous outposts were cobbled together with hand-held Motorolas and too few repeater stations […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c4eeb3f-e9fb-4618-974b-ab905f7e61f6",
                                                "sense_id": "1a0bbf21-e5c5-3e31-acf2-7686ac532e17",
                                                "text": "Francis, by contrast, was at pains to listen and act, going so far in 2023 as to call a curiously named synod on synodality in his anxiety to make the process work better as a conduit between the centre and the outposts of his global church."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff13f06d-d1f5-3002-a3e6-e5adab7668ca",
                                        "entry_id": "ff5e4005-f260-3bb2-a47c-09e420bdaba6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A square protected by a pawn that is in or near the enemy's stronghold."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9d9da58e-ed29-4aca-aefb-a5637507e410",
                        "source_entry_id": "8ec3142a-f714-339f-8780-24b2da2e8a8b",
                        "target_lang_word": "picket",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "picket",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "047eceea-951f-33e5-8af1-a28195c50c17",
                                        "entry_id": "b4e8cc90-fa48-3274-a088-9f4d04f5cbd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stake driven into the ground."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28f54652-aabc-4074-93d4-9417c568ebd6",
                                                "sense_id": "047eceea-951f-33e5-8af1-a28195c50c17",
                                                "text": "a picket fence"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "808929b2-6f57-3c7b-98d0-75266218d768",
                                        "entry_id": "b4e8cc90-fa48-3274-a088-9f4d04f5cbd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of punishment by which an offender had to rest his or her entire body weight on the top of a small stake."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "historical",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20e2b03d-1f46-316e-b87a-d093ff24cdc9",
                                        "entry_id": "b4e8cc90-fa48-3274-a088-9f4d04f5cbd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tool in mountaineering that is driven into the snow and used as an anchor or to arrest falls."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db272431-6190-3cb6-bf70-f8dbecf3b83b",
                                        "entry_id": "b4e8cc90-fa48-3274-a088-9f4d04f5cbd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One of the soldiers or troops placed on a line forward of a position to warn against an enemy advance; or any unit (for example, an aircraft or ship) performing a similar function."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60a4685f-edad-4ad9-a158-5c238c619f8a",
                                                "sense_id": "db272431-6190-3cb6-bf70-f8dbecf3b83b",
                                                "text": "So confident was he that he ignored the warning of his two British advisers to post pickets to watch the river, and even withdrew those they had placed there."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dfe1536d-2ac9-3619-a18a-e2edf3c5b640",
                                        "entry_id": "b4e8cc90-fa48-3274-a088-9f4d04f5cbd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sentry."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "sometimes",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "652c28f2-8c1d-483a-9cd5-70ef9853d5f0",
                                                "sense_id": "dfe1536d-2ac9-3619-a18a-e2edf3c5b640",
                                                "text": "Maccario, it was evident, did not care to take the risk of blundering upon a picket, and a man led them by twisting paths until at last the hacienda rose blackly before them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8304aa22-7782-3362-bc6b-9787c696bb92",
                                        "entry_id": "b4e8cc90-fa48-3274-a088-9f4d04f5cbd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A protester positioned outside an office, workplace etc. during a strike (usually in plural); also the protest itself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc09bede-ff93-468b-a325-2bb116321a16",
                                                "sense_id": "8304aa22-7782-3362-bc6b-9787c696bb92",
                                                "text": "Pickets normally endeavor to be non-violent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "017a3904-c60a-4d09-9ccc-9a4c5831b2df",
                                                "sense_id": "8304aa22-7782-3362-bc6b-9787c696bb92",
                                                "text": "In the autumn there was a row at some cement works about the unskilled labour men. A union had just been started for them and all but a few joined. One of these blacklegs was laid for by a picket and knocked out of time."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fee78ae-b04d-3209-af23-06251159081e",
                                        "entry_id": "b4e8cc90-fa48-3274-a088-9f4d04f5cbd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The card game piquet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "picket",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "208a3449-3a4a-3e5b-90eb-33be5852369b",
                                        "entry_id": "fc6c2e93-2ef9-39ed-91cd-385406c31afd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To protest, organized by a labour union, typically in front of the location of employment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ee38c66-9b15-3846-8d92-c1ae3037d8c8",
                                        "entry_id": "fc6c2e93-2ef9-39ed-91cd-385406c31afd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To enclose or fortify with pickets or pointed stakes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6b962e6-ae73-4207-9d6d-6f90e98bfd65",
                                                "sense_id": "2ee38c66-9b15-3846-8d92-c1ae3037d8c8",
                                                "text": "One of the most striking was the silver pin presented to all members of the National Women’s Party who served time for picketting the White House for women’s suffrage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "195f8a3c-b7d3-3fe0-b90c-58f06ebba218",
                                        "entry_id": "fc6c2e93-2ef9-39ed-91cd-385406c31afd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tether to, or as if to, a picket."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65e43d7f-fdb7-4971-a76c-aeb353169a02",
                                                "sense_id": "195f8a3c-b7d3-3fe0-b90c-58f06ebba218",
                                                "text": "to picket a horse"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "093dd58a-4176-4374-993f-f53a07a2eb2a",
                                                "sense_id": "195f8a3c-b7d3-3fe0-b90c-58f06ebba218",
                                                "text": "[T]he Moors kept a good Guard all Night, and did not unſaddle their Horſes, but picketted them before the Tent-Doors; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8f7e0cc-3184-4735-adca-5bb44c6bee06",
                                                "sense_id": "195f8a3c-b7d3-3fe0-b90c-58f06ebba218",
                                                "text": "[F]rom the outskirts of the fair, where are picketted the horses and the herds for sale, comes the tinkle of bells, a mule’s shrill scream, mingled with the music of a guitar or the rattle of castanets."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "155687ca-5421-3257-8c39-adef911cd13a",
                                        "entry_id": "fc6c2e93-2ef9-39ed-91cd-385406c31afd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To guard, as a camp or road, by an outlying picket."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28e0ae4a-c9f9-3f69-8436-36ea240912e0",
                                        "entry_id": "fc6c2e93-2ef9-39ed-91cd-385406c31afd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To torture by forcing to stand with one foot on a pointed stake."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
